Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Application Builder* position with Blink's Subs + AI team. At Sperse, I delivered customer-facing UX flows and UI components in React Flow and TypeScript that let users visually create, run, and monitor durable agent workflows. I also built a Python, LangGraph, LangChain, and FastAPI multi-agent CRM that securely routes requests across 40+ specialized agents for 10,000+ users. That combination of product-facing development and dependable backend delivery would help me contribute to Blink's mobile app features while collaborating closely with product and UX partners.

My work has consistently emphasized *code quality, maintainable features, and operational reliability*. I used Claude Code and Codex CLI to automate CI/CD pipelines, error monitoring, and automated testing, and built an AI-agent code-review pipeline that triages 25–30 pull requests each week while saving reviewers several hours. Earlier at Qualitest, I designed a Java and Spring Boot storage service spanning Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO, and used AWS Step Functions to prevent Lambda timeouts and improve error recovery across 100K+ weekly executions. These experiences align with Blink's need for object-oriented development, AWS services, full software development life cycle practices, and well-tested code.

I also built *TruthFlow Mobile Fit*, a public LangGraph and LangChain project that turns job requirements into traceable evidence mappings and refuses unsupported claims. Its five-stage workflow provides structured logging, validation, error handling, Markdown and JSON output, and a GitHub Actions quality gate backed by 14 passing unit and integration tests with 99% local statement coverage. The project reflects the same customer-focused, evidence-driven approach I would bring to Blink: inventing useful experiences, maintaining high standards, and building systems people can trust. Amazon's mission to make customers' lives better and easier through invention, together with its Customer Obsession and Invent and Simplify principles, strongly matches how I approach product engineering. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss the role and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your consideration; I look forward to connecting.

